      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Finally, using the above expression for $\\ell(z_{i}.\\,|\\,g_{f},\\,g_{m})$, averaging over all possible parental genotypes gives the unconditional likelihood for this family (Equation 13.11b). Assuming the QTL genotypes are in Hardy-Weinberg proportions, the unconditional likelihood has six unknown parameters: the three genotypic means, the allele frequency $p$, and the variances $\\sigma^{2}$ and $\\sigma_{c}^{2}$. Assuming the $n_{f}$ families in our pedigree are unrelated, the total likelihood is the product of the individual family likelihoods (Equation 13.13).",
      "source_page": 385,
      "printed_page": 365,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter13:p019:b5"
