    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A test for common-family effects but no major gene is given by the likelihood-ratio test using Equation 13.18 versus the likelihood function with $ \\sigma_c^2 = 0 $. The latter is just the likelihood function assuming a single underlying normal, which has its maximum value given by Equation 13.8. Likewise, the likelihood-ratio test for a major gene but no common-family effects uses the full likelihood and a restricted likelihood assuming $ \\sigma_c^2 = 0 $.",
